#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:0
msgid ""
"Turn on Mouse Keys to move the pointer and click using the numeric keypad if "
"you can't use a mouse or other pointing device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:7
msgid "Topics: Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:11
msgid "Click and move the mouse pointer using the keypad"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:13
msgid ""
"If you have difficulties using a mouse or other pointing device, you can "
"control the mouse pointer using the numeric keypad on your keyboard. This "
"feature is called **mouse keys**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:15
msgid "Open the Activities overview and start typing **accessibility**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:17
msgid ""
"You can access the Activities overview by pressing on it, by moving your "
"mouse pointer against the top-left corner of the screen, by using {kbd}"
"`Ctrl+Alt+Tab` followed by {kbd}`Enter`, or by using the {kbd}`Super` key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:19
msgid "Click {guilabel}`Accessibility` to open the panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:20
msgid "Open the {guilabel}`Pointing & Clicking` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:21
msgid "Enable the {guilabel}`Mouse Keys` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:22
msgid "Make sure that {kbd}`Num Lock` is turned off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:24
msgid "You will now be able to move the mouse pointer using the keypad."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:26
msgid ""
"The keypad is a set of numerical buttons on your keyboard, usually arranged "
"into a square grid. If you have a keyboard without a keypad (such as a "
"laptop keyboard), you may need to hold down the function ({kbd}`Fn`) key and "
"use certain other keys on your keyboard as a keypad. If you use this feature "
"often on a laptop, you can purchase external USB or Bluetooth numeric "
"keypads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:28
msgid ""
"Each number on the keypad corresponds to a direction. For example, pressing "
"{kbd}`8` will move the pointer upwards and pressing {kbd}`2` will move it "
"downwards. Press the {kbd}`5` key to click once with the mouse, or quickly "
"press it twice to double-click."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:30
msgid ""
"<!--\n"
"The list table doesn't really represent well what it renders as. A standard "
"Markdown table would be more visually readable:\n"
"\n"
"| 7 | 8 | 9 |\n"
"| 4 | 5 | 6 |\n"
"| 1 | 2 | 3 |\n"
"\n"
"However, this style of table requires a header, which we don't want here. "
"The list table is a workaround.\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""

