#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:62
msgid ""
"Most keyboards have a special key which allows you to right-click, sometimes "
"called the {kbd}`Menu` key. Note, however, that this key responds to where "
"your keyboard focus is, not where your mouse pointer is. See {ref}`simulate-"
"a-right-mouse-click` for information on how to right-click by holding down "
"{kbd}`5` or the left mouse button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:64
msgid ""
"If you want to use the keypad to type numbers while mouse keys is enabled, "
"turn {kbd}`Num Lock` on. The mouse cannot be controlled with the keypad when "
"{kbd}`Num Lock` is turned on, though."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/click-and-move-the-mouse-pointer-using-the-keypad.md:67
msgid ""
"The normal number keys, in a line at the top of the keyboard, will not "
"control the mouse pointer. Only the keypad number keys can be used."
msgstr ""
